article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Peter_and_St_Paul%27s_Church,_Shelford","cat":"SS Peter and Paul, Shelford","stories":[{"layer":"shelford","text":"By 1310–11 Shelford's church belonged to an Augustinian priory here. After Henry VIII dissolved the monasteries, the Stanhopes acquired the priory, in 1537, and with it the church. Lady Anne Stanhope's tomb, by Gabriel Royle, was put up after her death in 1588, and the family vault is dated 1677. In 1877–78 Lord Carnarvon paid for Ewan Christian to restore the church.","source":{"title":"Shelford St Peter and St Paul: history (Southwell and Nottingham Church History Project)","url":"https://southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk/shelford/hhistory.php","kind":"southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk","read":"2026-11-16"},"when":"1310","whenSrc":{"title":"Shelford St Peter and St Paul: history (Southwell and Nottingham Church History Project)","url":"https://southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk/shelford/hhistory.php","kind":"southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk","read":"2026-11-16"},"nm":"Shelford's church and priory"},{"layer":"shelford","text":"When Parliament's forces took Shelford House on 3 November 1645, Royalists led by a woman fired on them from the church tower; John Hutchinson had straw set alight to smoke them out, and smoke stains in the tower stairwell may date from then. Lady Anne Stanhope's monument and the font were damaged; the font was replaced in 1662.","source":{"title":"Shelford St Peter and St Paul: history (Southwell and Nottingham Church History Project)","url":"https://southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk/shelford/hhistory.php","kind":"southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk","read":"2026-11-16"},"weblinks":[["John Hutchinson","note:John Hutchinson"]],"links":["John Hutchinson"],"when":"1645","whenSrc":{"title":"Shelford St Peter and St Paul: history (Southwell and Nottingham Church History Project)","url":"https://southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk/shelford/hhistory.php","kind":"southwellchurches.nottingham.ac.uk","read":"2026-11-16"},"nm":"The siege in the tower","see":[["The storming of Shelford House","p735"]]}],"sum":"St Peter and St Paul's Church, Shelford is a parish church in the Church of England in Shelford, Nottinghamshire. The church is Grade II* listed by the Department for Digital, Culture, Media and Sport.","sumSrc":{"title":"St Peter and St Paul's Church, Shelford","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Peter_and_St_Paul%27s_Church%2C_Shelford"},"council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.016,52.97454]},"283321":{"h":10,"osm":"way/234014215","kind":"hall","sum":"Shelford Village Hall is a community centre on Church Street.","sumSrc":{"title":"OpenStreetMap","kind":"Written from the map's data"},"council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.01466,52.97436]},"283322":{"where":"West Street","h":10,"osm":"way/842076057","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.01594,52.9726]},"283323":{"where":"West Street","h":10,"osm":"way/842076058","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.0166,52.9732]},"283324":{"where":"Water Lane","h":10,"osm":"way/919979722","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.00959,52.97384]},"283325":{"h":10,"osm":"way/919979723","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.00911,52.97414]},"283326":{"h":10,"osm":"way/1309918065","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-0.98259,52.96325]},"283327":{"h":10,"osm":"way/98466872","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-0.98319,52.96373]},"283328":{"h":10,"osm":"way/98466967","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-0.98184,52.96331]},"283329":{"h":10,"osm":"way/1309915894","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-0.98216,52.96375]},"283330":{"h":8,"osm":"way/1457476512","kind":"house","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-0.97949,52.96279]},"283331":{"h":3,"osm":"way/1457494900","kind":"garage","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-0.97971,52.96249]},"283332":{"h":8,"osm":"way/1457494903","kind":"house","counci